# Chain: Delivery

ID: DL1
Parent: D0

Purpose:
  The full business-to-verified delivery flow — the stateful, immutable
  workflow that every delivery request follows. Business case is
  understood, requirements defined, business design shaped, decisions
  recorded, tasks broken down, behavior specified; then implementation
  branches execute in parallel, each through the same scoped
  review -> refactor -> security -> test pipeline (security pass
  PRECEDES per-branch tests — v2 ordering, Phase 155); the Final Test
  Suite closes the cross-layer loop; finally the whole flow is
  analyzed and verified. Step keys are canonical
  (bax ../workflow/step-keys.sdd).

Owns: chains/delivery.sdd

Flow:
  BC -> BR -> BD -> DS -> TK -> BDD
                              |
       +-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+
       |       |       |       |       |       |
       BE      DB      API     FE      MD      DC      (parallel branches)
       |       |       |       |       |       |
     CR-BE   CR-DB   CR-API  CR-FE   CR-MD   CR-DC     (scoped reviews)
       |       |       |       |       |       |
     RF-BE   RF-DB   RF-API  RF-FE   RF-MD   RF-DC     (scoped refactor,
       |       |       |       |       |       |        conditional — see
     SC-BE   SC-DB   SC-API  SC-FE   SC-MD   SC-DC     ImmutabilityRules
       |       |       |       |       |       |        note below)
     BE-TS   DB-TS   API-TS  FE-TS   MD-TS   DC-TS     (scoped security
       |       |       |       |       |       |        BEFORE branch
       +-------+-------+-------+-------+-------+        tests — v2)
                       |
                      FTS                                  (final test
                       |                                    suite: cross-
                       |                                    layer E2E)
                      AN -> VR

FlowNotation:
  short:  BC -> BR -> BD -> DS -> TK -> BDD -> [
    BE->CR-BE->RF-BE->SC-BE->BE-TS,
    DB->CR-DB->RF-DB->SC-DB->DB-TS,
    API->CR-API->RF-API->SC-API->API-TS,
    FE->CR-FE->RF-FE->SC-FE->FE-TS,
    MD->CR-MD->RF-MD->SC-MD->MD-TS,
    DC->CR-DC->RF-DC->SC-DC->DC-TS
    ] -> FTS -> AN -> VR
  canonical_keys: 24 base + RF-XX/SC-XX scoped aliases + FTS (bax
    ../workflow/step-keys.sdd — never redefined)

Dependencies:
  BR  -> [BC]
  BD  -> [BR]
  DS  -> [BD]
  TK  -> [DS]
  BDD -> [TK]
  BE  -> [BDD]
  DB  -> [BDD]
  API -> [BDD]
  FE  -> [BDD]
  MD  -> [BDD]
  DC  -> [BDD]
  CR-BE   -> [BE]
  CR-DB   -> [DB]
  CR-API  -> [API]
  CR-FE   -> [FE]
  CR-MD   -> [MD]
  CR-DC   -> [DC]
  RF-BE   -> [CR-BE]   (conditional — only if CR-BE raises change requests;
                        skipped if CR-BE passes clean)
  RF-DB   -> [CR-DB]   (conditional, same rule)
  RF-API  -> [CR-API]  (conditional, same rule)
  RF-FE   -> [CR-FE]   (conditional, same rule)
  RF-MD   -> [CR-MD]   (conditional, same rule)
  RF-DC   -> [CR-DC]   (conditional, same rule)
  SC-BE   -> [RF-BE]   (or [CR-BE] directly if RF-BE was skipped)
  SC-DB   -> [RF-DB]   (or [CR-DB] directly if RF-DB was skipped)
  SC-API  -> [RF-API]  (or [CR-API] directly if RF-API was skipped)
  SC-FE   -> [RF-FE]   (or [CR-FE] directly if RF-FE was skipped)
  SC-MD   -> [RF-MD]   (or [CR-MD] directly if RF-MD was skipped)
  SC-DC   -> [RF-DC]   (or [CR-DC] directly if RF-DC was skipped)
  BE-TS   -> [SC-BE]   (v2: branch tests only after scoped security pass)
  DB-TS   -> [SC-DB]   (v2, same rule)
  API-TS  -> [SC-API]  (v2, same rule)
  FE-TS   -> [SC-FE]   (v2, same rule)
  MD-TS   -> [SC-MD]   (v2, same rule)
  DC-TS   -> [SC-DC]   (v2, same rule)
  FTS     -> [BE-TS, DB-TS, API-TS, FE-TS, MD-TS, DC-TS]  (every ACTIVE
             branch's XX-TS — skipped branches excluded via StageSkip)
  AN  -> [FTS]
  VR  -> [AN]

Parallelism:
  The six branches (BE, DB, API, FE, MD, DC) execute in parallel after
  BDD; each branch follows the identical scoped sub-path
  CR-XX -> RF-XX -> SC-XX -> XX-TS — security validation precedes the
  branch's tests (v2, Phase 155): a security finding blocks the branch
  before any test effort is spent on defective code. AN waits for FTS
  (the Final Test Suite over all active branches' XX-TS). RF-XX is
  conditional: it only runs when CR-XX raises change requests, and is
  skipped when CR-XX passes clean (bax
  ../workflow/stages.sdd RFScopedSemantics). Branches not in a task's
  ImpactMatrix are skipped explicitly (never silently — bax
  transitions.sdd StageSkip).

ImmutabilityRules (flow protection):
  [DL1-1] The flow is IMMUTABLE: no skipping steps, no reordering, no
          executing future steps early. RF-XX's conditional skip is the
          one explicit exception — a clean CR-XX is a defined exit, not
          an omission.
  [DL1-2] Every /next continues from the SAVED STATE — the last completed
          step and the first incomplete step — never from conversation
          memory (bax ../runtime/state.sdd checkpoints).
  [DL1-3] Called 100 times, /next continues from the actual last state
          every time; restart from BC only when state explicitly requires.
  [DL1-4] A step is DONE only when: input exists, work completed, output
          artifact exists, internally consistent, validation passed —
          never on assumption (bax ../tasks/DONE-PROOF.sdd).
  [DL1-5] A blocking BUG stops the current step and the flow — no
          continuation until resolved (bax ../tasks/BUG-REGISTRY.sdd).
  [DL1-6] VR = VERIFIED is reachable only when all required steps are
          complete (including each branch's SC-XX and XX-TS, plus FTS)
          AND no blocking BUG remains.
  [DL1-7] FLOW VERSIONING (v2, Phase 155): persisted runs whose state
          carries no flow_version are v1 runs under the OLD
          XX-TS -> SC-XX ordering. They are DEPRECATED — /next MUST
          re-initialize the run, never resume a v1 run under the v2
          ordering (delivery-runner enforces via flow_version field).
  [DL1-8] FTS (Final Test Suite) is MANDATORY for every delivery run:
          cross-layer E2E, integration, and regression over all ACTIVE
          branches. Skipping FTS is possible only through an explicit
          StageSkip with recorded reason — never silently.

StepState (persisted per delivery run):
  storage: .specdd/delivery/{run_id}/state.sdd (runtime-only)
  fields: run_id, current_step, completed_steps[], first_incomplete,
    branch_states{key -> state}, rf_skipped{key -> bool}, blocking_bugs[],
    last_checkpoint, flow_version (2; absent => v1 deprecated run, bax
    [DL1-7]), deprecated_from (set when a v1 run is re-initialized)
  resume: /next reads this state FIRST; completed steps are never
    re-executed ([RT8-RT9] checkpoint discipline).

Retry: 3

Navigation:
  StepKeys: @../workflow/step-keys.sdd
  Stages: @../workflow/stages.sdd
  Transitions: @../workflow/transitions.sdd
  TaskStateMachine: @../tasks/TASK-STATE-MACHINE.sdd
  BugRegistry: @../tasks/BUG-REGISTRY.sdd
  NextCommand: @../commands/sdd-next.sdd
  Checkpoints: @../runtime/state.sdd

